{
  "mn11:0.1": "Middle Discourses 11 ",
  "mn11:0.2": "The Shorter Discourse on the Lion’s Roar ",
  "mn11:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn11:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn11:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn11:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn11:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn11:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn11:2.1": "“‘Only here is there a true ascetic, here a second ascetic, here a third ascetic, and here a fourth ascetic. ",
  "mn11:2.2": "Other sects are empty of ascetics.’ ",
  "mn11:2.3": "This, mendicants, is how you should rightly roar your lion’s roar. ",
  "mn11:3.1": "It’s possible that wanderers of other religions might say: ",
  "mn11:3.2": "‘But what is the source of the venerables’ certainty and forcefulness that they say this?’ ",
  "mn11:3.3": "",
  "mn11:3.4": "",
  "mn11:3.5": "You should say to them: ",
  "mn11:3.6": "‘There are four things explained by the Blessed One, who knows and sees, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha. Seeing these things in ourselves we say that: ",
  "mn11:3.7": "“Only here is there a true ascetic, here a second ascetic, here a third ascetic, and here a fourth ascetic. ",
  "mn11:3.8": "Other sects are empty of ascetics.” ",
  "mn11:3.9": "What four? ",
  "mn11:3.10": "We have confidence in the Teacher, we have confidence in the teaching, and we have fulfilled the precepts. ",
  "mn11:3.11": "A